WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.445 --> 00:00:17.374
On Tuesday afternoon Daisy and Kaleem were going to visit Scamp.

2
00:00:19.816 --> 00:00:22.077
"I'm coming with you," Beatrice said.

3
00:00:22.097 --> 00:00:24.399
"I need to keep an eye on you."

4
00:00:24.419 --> 00:00:26.961
"Huh? What do you mean?"

5
00:00:27.401 --> 00:00:28.181
Daisy asked.

6
00:00:28.201 --> 00:00:31.564
"Um, just so you're safe," Beatrice said.

7
00:00:33.696 --> 00:00:34.556
Daisy shrugged.

8
00:00:34.576 --> 00:00:36.057
"Grace will be there.

9
00:00:36.517 --> 00:00:38.218
So you're going to have to be careful."

10
00:00:39.439 --> 00:00:41.660
Beatrice landed on Daisy's headband.

11
00:00:41.680 --> 00:00:44.981
"Kaleem said I look like his mother's pin, remember?

12
00:00:45.922 --> 00:00:47.262
So I'll stay right here.

13
00:00:47.942 --> 00:00:51.084
If Grace notices me, tell her I'm just a decoration."

14
00:00:51.104 --> 00:00:55.306
"Okay, but make sure you stay very still.

15
00:00:56.186 --> 00:00:59.127
Pins don't usually move—or buzz either!"

16
00:01:06.912 --> 00:01:08.693
The kids walked Scamp and fed him.

17
00:01:11.133 --> 00:01:12.814
They also refilled his pool.

18
00:01:17.755 --> 00:01:20.356
Scamp barked, splashing around happily.

19
00:01:20.376 --> 00:01:24.317
"I love playing in the water!"

20
00:01:26.097 --> 00:01:27.237
Grace looked worried.

21
00:01:27.257 --> 00:01:29.178
"He keeps barking.

22
00:01:29.198 --> 00:01:31.519
Do you think he's lonely?"

23
00:01:31.539 --> 00:01:35.060
"He's happy to be in the water," Daisy said.

24
00:01:35.080 --> 00:01:37.372
"He loves—" "Bzz!"

25
00:01:38.533 --> 00:01:40.194
Beatrice made a warning sound.

26
00:01:40.214 --> 00:01:43.416
"I'm thirsty," Kaleem said quickly.

27
00:01:43.436 --> 00:01:45.237
"Let's go get milkshakes."

28
00:01:45.977 --> 00:01:47.378
Grace looked disappointed.

29
00:01:47.398 --> 00:01:49.059
"That sounds fun.

30
00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:51.320
But I can't go.

31
00:01:51.340 --> 00:01:54.702
I have to clean the filter on my fish tank."

32
00:01:55.663 --> 00:01:59.085
"I never knew owning fish was so complicated," Kaleem said.

33
00:01:59.725 --> 00:02:00.526
Grace sighed.

34
00:02:00.546 --> 00:02:04.408
"It's a big responsibility.

35
00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:07.142
Sometimes there's too much to do."

36
00:02:13.427 --> 00:02:17.410
She said good-bye, and Daisy and Kaleem set off for the ice cream parlor.

37
00:02:25.497 --> 00:02:28.680
Halfway there, they saw a rabbit running down the sidewalk.

38
00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:30.641
She looked terrified.

39
00:02:30.661 --> 00:02:32.623
"What's wrong?"

40
00:02:32.863 --> 00:02:33.564
Daisy called.

41
00:02:34.144 --> 00:02:35.906
The rabbit skidded to a stop.

42
00:02:37.867 --> 00:02:39.208
"I just saw a monster!

43
00:02:39.228 --> 00:02:43.111
It roared like a horrible, angry beast!"

44
00:02:45.313 --> 00:02:47.355
A bird swooped close to Daisy.

45
00:02:47.375 --> 00:02:50.757
"You're the girl who can talk to animals!

46
00:02:51.458 --> 00:02:52.879
We've all heard about you.

47
00:02:53.840 --> 00:02:55.201
I saw a monster too.

48
00:02:56.062 --> 00:02:57.943
It had shaggy fur like a bear!"

49
00:02:59.304 --> 00:03:01.586
Daisy told Kaleem what the animals had said.

50
00:03:02.367 --> 00:03:03.648
Kaleem scratched his head.

51
00:03:04.817 --> 00:03:06.038
"How strange.

52
00:03:07.098 --> 00:03:08.399
What do you think they saw?"

53
00:03:10.201 --> 00:03:12.562
Just then a dog barked loudly.

54
00:03:12.582 --> 00:03:15.444
"Monster! Monster!"

55
00:03:15.945 --> 00:03:16.705
the dog said.

56
00:03:16.725 --> 00:03:19.007
"There's a monster on the loose!"

57
00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:24.551
Daisy looked over the fence at the dog.

58
00:03:24.571 --> 00:03:27.373
"Did you see the monster that looks like a bear?"

59
00:03:27.393 --> 00:03:31.316
"I don't know what a bear is," the beagle said.

60
00:03:32.224 --> 00:03:37.468
"The monster I saw had a long, strange neck like a giant, furry snake!"

61
00:03:41.431 --> 00:03:42.792
A cat wandered past.

62
00:03:42.812 --> 00:03:46.095
"Was the monster as tall as a house?

63
00:03:46.996 --> 00:03:48.657
Because I saw that monster too.

64
00:03:49.998 --> 00:03:51.739
I've never seen anything like it!"

65
00:03:55.882 --> 00:03:57.484
A butterfly fluttered past.

66
00:03:59.884 --> 00:04:00.825
"Be careful!

67
00:04:01.065 --> 00:04:04.088
There's a monster around, and it shoots something out of its mouth.

68
00:04:04.528 --> 00:04:05.729
It might be poison!"

69
00:04:08.391 --> 00:04:10.093
Daisy filled in Kaleem again.

70
00:04:10.113 --> 00:04:12.314
"A monster?

71
00:04:13.015 --> 00:04:14.536
Here?" Kaleem said.

72
00:04:14.556 --> 00:04:19.861
"Kaleem, there's no such thing as monsters," Daisy said.

73
00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:21.642
Kaleem grinned.

74
00:04:21.662 --> 00:04:25.105
"I didn't believe people could talk to animals until recently.

75
00:04:25.705 --> 00:04:26.466
But now I do.

76
00:04:27.247 --> 00:04:28.548
Maybe monsters are real too!"

77
00:04:29.696 --> 00:04:30.797
Daisy shook her head.

78
00:04:31.337 --> 00:04:33.279
She didn't think that monsters were real.

79
00:04:34.179 --> 00:04:37.502
But she was sure the animals had seen something strange.

80
00:04:37.522 --> 00:04:40.364
"Where did you see this monster?"

81
00:04:40.704 --> 00:04:41.765
she asked the animals.

82
00:04:41.785 --> 00:04:45.507
"It stomped past my fence," the dog said.

83
00:04:45.527 --> 00:04:48.009
"I saw it heading that way."

84
00:04:48.870 --> 00:04:50.611
The cat gestured down the street.

85
00:04:53.453 --> 00:04:54.914
Daisy beckoned to Kaleem.

86
00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:57.796
"Let's go that way—and investigate!"
